      "writtenOn": "2026-07-28T14:06:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "docker_tag \u003d $2\n\nEVSSIM_RUN_SUDO\u003dy evssim_run \"$docker_tag\" \"/scripts/image-maker/${vm_version}.sh\"\nEVSSIM_RUN_SUDO\u003dy evssim_run \"$docker_tag\" chown -R external:external $EVSSIM_DIST_FOLDER\n\n\nUsing VERSION_QEMU_IMAGE for the Docker container tag wich translates to 2.X.y ot 11.0 is deceiving. If build-qemu-image.sh is using a container of a specific version, it should be loaded by load_config.sh from the version configuration JSON.",
